Point "added to the browser" at the button the shell drew.

Installing an extension ends with a bubble pointing at the extension's
toolbar button, or at the extensions button when it has none of its own.
With the shell drawing the browser there is no Chromium toolbar to point at:
GetExtensionsContainerViews() finds nothing, and the dialog fell through to
a browser-modal box in the middle of the window.

The shell draws those buttons and already reports where they are, under the
two names Chromium's own rule distinguishes -- "extension:<id>" and
"extensions". Nothing read them: GetAuraShellAnchorRect() has been in the
bridge, with a comment describing exactly this, and no caller. This is the
caller.

The fallback order matches desktop's: the extension's own button first,
the extensions button when it is not pinned, and the modal box when the
shell has reported neither.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/extensions/extension_dialog_utils_views.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/extensions/extension_dialog_utils_views.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/extensions/extension_dialog_utils_views.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/extensions/extension_dialog_utils_views.cc
@@ -12,7 +12,61 @@
 #include "ui/views/bubble/bubble_dialog_model_host.h"
 #include "ui/views/widget/widget.h"
 
+#include "build/build_config.h"
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+#include "base/strings/strcat.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/ui/ohos/aura_shell_runtime_bridge.h"  // nogncheck
+#include "ui/aura/window.h"
+#include "ui/aura/window_tree_host.h"
+#endif
+
 namespace {
+
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+// Where the shell drew the button this bubble should point at.
+//
+// With the shell drawing the browser there is no Chromium toolbar, so there
+// is no ExtensionsContainerViews and no anchor view -- and the dialog fell
+// back to a browser-modal box in the middle of the window, which is not what
+// "added to the browser" should look like.
+//
+// The shell does draw those buttons and reports where they are, under the
+// same two names Chromium's own rule distinguishes: one extension points at
+// that extension's button, anything else at the extensions button. Falls
+// back from the first to the second, because an extension that is not
+// pinned has no button of its own -- which is what
+// GetReferenceButtonForPopup() does on desktop.
+//
+// Empty when the shell has said nothing, and then the modal is still right.
+gfx::Rect GetOhosShellAnchorRect(
+    gfx::NativeWindow parent,
+    const std::vector<extensions::ExtensionId>& extension_ids) {
+  if (!parent || !chrome::ohos::IsAuraShellChromeHiddenByShell()) {
+    return gfx::Rect();
+  }
+  aura::Window* const root = parent->GetRootWindow();
+  if (!root || !root->GetHost()) {
+    return gfx::Rect();
+  }
+  const gfx::AcceleratedWidget widget = root->GetHost()->GetAcceleratedWidget();
+
+  gfx::Rect rect;
+  if (extension_ids.size() == 1) {
+    rect = chrome::ohos::GetAuraShellAnchorRect(
+        widget, base::StrCat({"extension:", extension_ids[0]}));
+  }
+  if (rect.IsEmpty()) {
+    rect = chrome::ohos::GetAuraShellAnchorRect(widget, "extensions");
+  }
+  if (rect.IsEmpty()) {
+    return rect;
+  }
+  // The shell reports the button in its window's own coordinates; a bubble
+  // anchors in screen ones.
+  rect.Offset(root->GetBoundsInScreen().OffsetFromOrigin());
+  return rect;
+}
+#endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
 
